<!--
    kuna infrastructure test: restart observability (roadmap item 5).

    Mechanism (c) - global restart with persisted hints - is the most
    diagnostic feedback signal in the engine.  This test exercises the
    `restarts` command + the kuna restart recorder.

    HISTORY (assertion #1 removed, 2026-06-22): the original #1 reused the
    upstream switchmulti binary on the premise that its jump table is only
    partially recovered during flow analysis, so upstream's
    JumpTable::recoverLabels installs an Override::insertMultistageJump hint
    and RESTARTS the function (stage-model edge 2) to finish recovery, and
    the kuna recorder logged that hint.  That premise no longer holds in kuna:
    kuna's value/flow analysis recovers switchmulti's FULL 7-entry table in a
    SINGLE pass (verified: `restarts` reports none, and the upstream
    switchmulti datatest, which checks all 7 case bodies, passes).  The
    multistage restart that #1 was built to observe is an upstream two-pass
    recovery artifact that kuna's more-complete one-pass recovery makes
    unnecessary; reproducing it would mean regressing that (correct) recovery.
    (The multistage-restart WIRING in JumpTable::matchModel/checkForMultistage
    is also still a documented W4 SEAM.)  So #1 was discarded as obsolete:
    not a port regression to fix, but a test of a path kuna no longer takes.

    #2 still asserts the empty path on a function that never restarts (gh558
    bytes at the second symbol); the recorder + `restarts` command remain valid.
-->
